        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 11000,
      "caption": "The VNDK is the set of system libraries vendor code may use, versioned with the vendor image.",
      "narration": "The VNDK is a curated set of system libraries vendor code may use. LL-NDK libraries like libc and liblog stay in place; the rest ship in vndk directories.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "What vendor may link",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "LL-NDK: libc, libm, libdl, liblog",
            "VNDK: /system/lib64/vndk-<ver>",
            "vendor's own /vendor/lib64"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 24,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Everything else in /system/lib64 is private",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "red",
          "at": 5500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "At runtime the dynamic linker resolves libraries per namespace from /linkerconfig/ld.config.txt.",
      "narration": "At runtime the linker resolves libraries per namespace. A config file lists search paths and which libraries each namespace may reach through links.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Linker namespaces",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "ini",
          "text": "[vendor]\nnamespace.default.search.paths =\n  /vendor/${LIB}\nnamespace.default.links = system\nnamespace.default.link.system.\n  shared_libs = libc.so:libm.so:...",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 26,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 4500,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Config lives at /linkerconfig/ld.config.txt",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 10,
          "color": "gray",
          "at": 6000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Soong also enforces it at build time with vendor_available, vndk and vendor properties.",
      "narration": "Soong enforces the same rule at build time. A vendor module can only link libraries marked vendor available or VNDK, otherwise the build fails.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Build-time wall",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "cc_library {\n    name: \"libshared\",\n    vendor_available: true,\n    vndk: { enabled: true },\n}",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 20,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 20,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "hl",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 3500,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "vendor: true modules link only these libraries",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 46,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
          "color": "green",
          "at": 5000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "takeaway": "Treble enforces library boundaries twice: Soong rejects illegal links at build time and linker namespaces refuse them at runtime.",
